3. Uncertainty and limitations 

The cited studies demonstrate these inferences only for specific systems (US/PS, VUV/sulfite, particular photocatalysts) and pH ranges, so the identified “dominant” species cannot be generalized to all PFOA treatments. Scavengers are not perfectly selective and can perturb the system (e.g., by changing ionic strength or light absorption), so mechanistic assignments from scavenger tests alone are approximate and usually need corroboration (e.g., ESR, product analysis).

